                <pb facs="0631" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg551"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Russell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States to Venezuela</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">San Juan, P. R.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Russell reports that a revolutionary force from Colombia, commanded by an
                    important Venezuelan, Rangel Garbiras, is invading Venezuela, which Government
                    has sent 10,000 men to meet the invading force, and that all individual
                    guaranties under the constitution have been suspended by the President of
                    Venezuela.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
